  "findings": [
    "Final 512-sample views preserve silver objective barrels, braided fiber reflections, curved black-housing highlights, stage self-reflections, contact shadows, and soft cast shadows.",
    "Text labels, objective color bands, and micrometer knurling remain readable; the final two-stage denoiser avoids the blocky enlargement seen in the early prototype.",
    "All six final views use 1245 by 1020 actual ray-traced pixels and 512 samples, with the photographed instrument pose paused. No static Blender still is substituted.",
    "Raw and filtered captures use the same completed 512-sample radiance buffer. Display contrast is applied equally to both.",
    "Current live-mode screenshots and all final photo captures match the current published source file fingerprints."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Photo quality is progressive and pauses physics; camera motion restarts refinement, and instrument controls return to Interactive.",
    "The still image remains a separate Blender Cycles render. Browser materials approximate anisotropic finishes, use a finite bounce budget and a simpler denoiser, and retain some fine sampling noise.",
    "Timing evidence is from an A100 GPU at the recorded viewport and is not a performance guarantee for visitors. The gallery and ordinary interactive mode do not require the path tracer."
